-- PERMANENT negative control, NARROWED 2026-07-26.
--
-- A negated numeral literal now lands in Integer whenever a signed carrier
-- is reachable — `-1` means the integer −1, and the ℕ→ℤ→ℚ→ℝ coercions carry
-- it on to whatever the position wants (locked by `Test/negative_numeral`).
-- That reverses this file's original claim, from PLAN_ELABORATOR_ERGONOMICS
-- step E0, that `-1` with nothing to supply a carrier must stay rejected: a
-- literal has no intrinsic type, so there is nothing to invent.
--
-- What this file now locks: with **no signed carrier in scope at all** — no
-- `Integer.negate`, no coercion into one — the operator still has nowhere to
-- go, and says so naming the carrier it was left holding. Only `Natural` is
-- imported here.
--
-- The companion control `unseeded_negative_natural.math` kept its full
-- strength: a negated Natural VARIABLE is rejected even with the whole tower
-- in scope, because `m` already has a type and reading `-m` as an integer
-- would drift an ℕ expression into ℤ unasked.
module ErrorTest.unseeded_negative_numeral

import Natural.basics
import Natural.arithmetic

definition ErrorTest.control : Proposition := -1 = -1
